  "result": "`drv.motion.stopped` passed the gate with `OK` on the first run, using 1 of the 6 allowed runs.\n\n**Concept body:** `.cmp (.measure \"kin_speed\" [x]) .le (.param \"tol\")`. A road user counts as halted when its speed is at or below `tol`, judged at one observation only. The contract states the atom, the comparison and the parameter, so I made no reading choices and declared no narrowings.\n\n**Witnesses:** the instance sets `tol` to 0.2 m/s. Track 1 is a car at (0, 0) heading east, with no structures or devices, over 3 instants 1 s apart.\n- **holds:** speed 0.05 m/s, compliant.\n- **fails:** speed 2 m/s, with the car moving 2 m each second, violated.\n- **blind:** the holds scene with the car's speed left unobserved and `kin.speed` left out of the manifest, unknown.\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
